# Binary files — never let Git touch these bytes (line-ending conversion,
# text auto-detection) or they get silently corrupted on checkout. This
# is exactly what happened on Windows: fraud_model.pkl loaded fine on
# macOS but threw "input stream corrupted" on Windows, because Git's
# default CRLF conversion mangled the pickle's raw binary content.
*.pkl binary
*.joblib binary
*.npy binary
*.npz binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.mov binary
*.mp4 binary
